one-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-20T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Broomfield, CO; Douglas, CO; Denver, CO; Weld, CO; Boulder, CO; Jefferson, CO; Larimer, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.34156115e6b0d467e8b45dc0f7f2b946c514cada.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.34156115e6b0d467e8b45dc0f7f2b946c514cada.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-20T06:13:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 200613 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1213 AM MDT Thu Aug 20 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Summer heat and drier Thursday into Friday, although isolated showers/storms in the mountains. - Monsoon moisture returns this weekend and holds into early next week, with increasing chance of storms. && .DISCUSSION /Through Wednesday/... Issued at 1242 P","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-19T18:56:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Thursday... Isolated to scattered showers and storms (greatest coverage from Summit and Park Counties into southern Lincoln County) will end early this evening. Good humidity recovery is expected overnight in all but the foothills and thermal belts in the mountains where only moderate recovery is expected. Mostly dry and warmer weather will develop Thursday as a","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"lsl01","station_name":"La Salle","distance_km":7,"soil_temp_5cm_f":69.69,"soil_temp_15cm_f":71.1,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_